{
  "status": "ok",
  "data": {
    "query": "China currency manipulator designation August 2019 implications",
    "search_window": {
      "from": "2019-07-08",
      "to": "2019-08-07"
    },
    "sources": {
      "grounding": {
        "generic": [
          {
            "url": "https://www.usnews.com/news/world-report/articles/2019-08-06/currency-manipulator-label-signals-further-escalation-of-us-china-trade-war",
            "title": "‘Currency Manipulator’ Label Signals Further Escalation of ...",
            "snippets": [
              "# ‘Currency Manipulator’ Label Signals Further Escalation of U.S.-China Trade War\nThe label imposed by the Trump administration is mostly symbolic, but the designation – and China’s reaction to it – signal that a resolution to the ongoing trade dispute is growing more distant.",
              "China's central bank on Tuesday warned that the Treasury Department's recent decision to designate Beijing a \"currency manipulator\" would \"seriously undermine the international financial order\" and \"trigger financial market turmoil,\" as neither American nor Chinese officials show any signs of backing down from their ongoing trade dispute.",
              "The People's Bank of China said in a statement Tuesday that President Donald Trump's administration \"disregards the facts and unreasonably affixes China with the label of 'currency manipulators,' which is a behavior that harms others and oneself.\"\n\nTreasury on Monday evening slapped China with the manipulator distinction – a move that in itself is viewed as mostly symbolic but could allow Trump to politically justify the implementation of even more tariffs in the months ahead",
              "### Political Cartoons on Tariffs and Trade\n\"The specific implications of that move are not the biggest thing. The bigger point is that this is another escalating step whereby these two countries seem to be diverging further rather than making some attempts at finding some way out,\" says Louis Kuijs, the Hong Kong-based chief Asia economist at Oxford Economics. \"It makes it more likely we'll see further escalation.\"",
              "Trump has long threatened to label China a currency manipulator, suggesting that Beijing takes action to inflate or devalue the strength of its yuan currency to fit political or economic agendas",
              "And experts agree that China has in the past influenced its currency in a way that more open Western economies would not. Former President Bill Clinton last slapped the manipulator distinction on China in 1994, though more recent presidents have held back from using the label.",
              "A cheap yuan makes Chinese exports more attractive to international buyers, while imports into China become relatively more expensive. China on Monday allowed its yuan currency to drop in value to its lowest level against the dollar in more than a decade – specifically acknowledging that the move was in part a response to the Trump administration's latest round of tariff threats. By the end of the day, Treasury issued a statement warning that Beijing was trying to \"gain unfair competitive advantage in international trade.\"",
              "China's decision to allow the yuan to depreciate Monday sent international stock and currency markets reeling. The Dow Jones Industrial Average closed down more than 500 points as investors reacted to the world's two largest economies butting heads",
              "\"Internationally, this led to quite a bit of upheaval in currency markets,\" Kuijs says. \"Any movement in the Chinese currency will lead to much bigger moves in other currencies. This is a really sensitive area.\"",
              "Ironically, China's currency devaluation was dictated in large part by market forces. Kuijs notes that China does not want to be seen as the instigator of economic instability, so it had actually been propping up its yuan currency rather than allowing it to depreciate against the dollar – a natural economic consequence of Trump's tariff implementation",
              "Though Treasury labeled China a currency manipulator, the drop in the yuan's value came in part because Chinese officials pulled back on their manipulation.\n\nMORE:\n\nIran Oil Stockpiles Swell as Sanctions Tighten\n\n\"What they did yesterday was to take their hands off the currency while pressure was imposed on its currency by President Trump and the escalation of the trade war,\" Kuijs says",
              "But experts are expecting further retaliation in the months ahead, as the margin continues to narrow for a productive solution that allows both American and Chinese officials to save face"
            ]
          },
          {
            "url": "https://www.cnbc.com/2019/08/05/us-treasury-designates-china-as-a-currency-manipulator.html",
            "title": "US Treasury designates China as a currency manipulator",
            "snippets": [
              "# US declares China a currency manipulator, says it's using yuan to gain 'unfair advantage' in trade\nThe U.S. Treasury Department on Monday designated China as currency manipulator, a historic move that no White House had exercised since the Clinton administration.\n\n\"Secretary Mnuchin, under the auspices of President Trump, has today determined that China is a Currency Manipulator,\" the Treasury Department said in a release. \"As a result of this determination, Secretary Mnuchin will engage with the International Monetary Fund to eliminate the unfair competitive advantage created by China's latest actions.\"",
              "The formal designation — the first since President Bill Clinton's administration in 1994 — came after China on Monday allowed its currency to breach a psychological level. The yuan fell to 7 against the dollar earlier in the session for the first time since 2008",
              "\"In recent days, China has taken concrete steps to devalue its currency, while maintaining substantial foreign exchange reserves despite active use of such tools in the past,\" the Treasury Department added. \"The context of these actions and the implausibility of China's market stability rationale confirm that the purpose of China's currency devaluation is to gain unfair competitive advantage in international trade.\"",
              "Until Monday, the Trump administration had passed on five opportunities to label China as a currency manipulator. The most recent opportunity occurred in May, when Treasury officials decided China had not met the criteria required to label it a manipulator.",
              "\"I think many people in the private sector may not conclude it is a currency manipulator. The key rule is it's not intervening consistently or persistently to weaken the currency and therefore the private sector, like economists and strategists may not be convinced,\" said Marc Chandler, chief market strategist at Bannockburn",
              "\"This is another step in the currency war,\" he added. \"This also makes trade more difficult. This is probably bi-partisan. Many Republicans and Democrats think china is taking advantage of us.\"\n\nEven before the formal designation, President Donald Trump took to Twitter to voice his opinion, accusing Beijing of manipulating its currency as the trade war between the world's largest economies intensified",
              "\"China dropped the price of their currency to an almost a historic low,\" Trump said in a tweet. \"It's called 'currency manipulation.' Are you listening Federal Reserve? This is a major violation which will greatly weaken China over time!\"\n\ntweet\n\nThat drew support from the other side of the political aisle on Monday, when Senate Democratic Leader Chuck Schumer supported designating China a currency manipulator",
              "\"China has been manipulating their currency long-before and since President Trump took office,\" the New York politician said in a statement. \"He should finally tell his Treasury Secretary to label China a currency manipulator. That's all he needs to do to make it happen.\"",
              "The next step is for the U.S. to make its case to the IMF, but it's not likely to lead to formal penalties. The manipulator label is mostly symbolic and matters more as a slight to one of the United States' biggest creditors and an escalation in the trade war.\n\nThe Treasury Department's announcement centered around a 1988 portion of federal law that permits the U.S. Treasury Secretary to work with the IMF to \"eliminate the unfair advantage\" associated with currency manipulation",
